# Prefer F: Drive

- **Never** clone repos, download installers, create caches, unpack archives, or install **skills/plugins** onto `C:` (including `~/.claude/skills`, `%USERPROFILE%`, `%TEMP%` on C).
- Skills always land under `F:\tools\<repo>/` and are linked into `F:\GBGCL\.claude\skills\` (or other `F:\` project paths). Never `cp` into `C:\Users\...\ .claude\skills`.
- Prefer `F:\` paths (e.g. `F:\tools\`, `F:\GBGCL\`, or project-local dirs under this repo).
- Redirect `$env:TEMP` / `$env:TMP` → `F:\tools\tmp` for any download/extract work.
- `C:` is often near-full; treat writes there as last resort and warn the user first.
- When the user says install skills with default permissions / no confirmation: proceed without asking.
